Two main reasons:
1) Keeping the meanness of monsters and traps down. It's nice to be able to
have magic resistance before it is possible for the dungeon to generate a
poly trap.
2) Protection racket, to make buying protection easier by keeping the price
down. Spending 400 gold per point is a lot less effort than spending 1600
per point. I've had characters have to wait until halfway through Gehennom
before being able to buy protection because there wasn't enough gold
available earlier (a game without Ludios can have issues in this regard).

> Though there was a level the other day full of nymphs, 
>leprechauns, and monkeys all stealing my gear and money.  I could have 
>skipped that one. 

Nothing compels you to stay on such a level if you have the means to get
out of it quickly. Leprechauns aren't a HUGE deal, but a bunch of nymphs
can (indirectly) kill you with amazing efficiency.


